smartcrop.js — vendored third-party dependency
==============================================

Upstream:  https://github.com/jwagner/smartcrop.js
Source:    https://unpkg.com/smartcrop@2.0.5/smartcrop.js
Vendored:  src/shared/vendor/smartcrop.cjs
Version:   2.0.5 (published 2021-09-01)
Size:      17674 bytes, 594 lines
SHA-256:   fbc74cd1edd245b335af2404b5b55e29dca3f0c22053a4b6027df1ae05c340c7

The file is stored with a .cjs extension. The contents are byte-identical to
upstream — only the extension differs, so the hash below still verifies. The
extension is required: the file is CommonJS (it ends in `module.exports`), and
Vite's CommonJS interop only processes node_modules by default, so a .js file
here is parsed as ESM and the default import fails to resolve at build time.
The .cjs extension makes both the dev server and the Rollup build treat it as
CommonJS. Its type declarations are therefore in smartcrop.d.cts, which is where
TypeScript looks for a .cjs module under moduleResolution "Bundler".

This file is vendored rather than installed from npm. The package has had no
release since September 2021, so a dependency would buy no future patches while
leaving an open supply-chain edge. The copy here is frozen at the version that
was reviewed.

The SHA-256 above was verified identical between the npm artifact and the public
GitHub source, ruling out a published tarball that differs from the reviewed
repository. Re-verify with:

    sha256sum src/shared/vendor/smartcrop.js

Replacing this file means re-reviewing it and updating the hash above. Do not
upgrade it casually.


